15a3536d3e7577b0466389aabfb011","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-on.1/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-11-21T17:17:08.409557+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-on.1","local_name":"bob-cli-on.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-on","agent_clan_generation":"20261121111434","bead_id":"bob-cli-on.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-on[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Task requirements (reqs)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]A task can carry requirements: checkbox children without `#task`, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]nested as deep as the work needs, drawn as a quiet ⌗⌗ run in the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]task's ink. They are met when the task closes and can never be [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]ticked early. They can be dropped with a reason or carried into [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]their own task, and the close card audits them once. They sit in [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]one canonical block order beside a NOTES drawer, and they promote [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]one level at a time into project tasks. bob-cli, bob-plugins, Bob [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Mac Capture, and the vault agree byte for byte through shared [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]vectors, and every legacy REQUIREMENTS drawer becomes NOTES.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]17[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]task_requirements.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/task_requirements.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-on[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-on/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Requirement recognizer, shared vectors, and the contract page[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]req-contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]req-contract: retire the bob-cli-of epic, then add the recursive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]requirement recognizer in bob-cli with its derived state model, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]structural row identity, RQ vectors, the TaskChildKind::Requirement [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]variant, and the docs/task-requirements.md contract.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Keep every task reader and outside-text writer off requirement[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]lines[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]reader-hardening[dim] · [dim][/dim]after req-contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reader-hardening: make projects sync, embedded-tree closes, loss and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]clobber guards, agenda, dataview emulation, archive moves, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lane/walk/stats counts treat only real #task lines as tasks; escape [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pasted checkboxes from gcal, gkeep, gmail, and highlights writers; add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the offer-close SV case.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The task block layout module and requirement line writers[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]block-layout[dim] · [dim][/dim]after req-contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]block-layout: add task_block_layout (zones, insertion slots, tidy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]planning, the NOTES rule) and the pure [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]drop/restore/toggle/first-requirement writers with RL and RW vectors, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]then route ensure_drawer and capture note placement through it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The bob task tidy command[/bold #D7AFFF]                                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]task-tidy[dim] · [dim][/dim]after block-layout[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]task-tidy: add `bob task tidy`, a previewed, one-commit repair of open [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]task blocks into canonical order that moves whole subtrees and files [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]loose notes of requirement-owning tasks into NOTES.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The bob task rename-drawer command[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]drawer-rename[dim] · [dim][/dim]after task-tidy[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]drawer-rename: add `bob task rename-drawer OLD NEW`, a previewed, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]idempotent, one-commit rename and merge of task drawers and ^prj H2 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]drawer sections across the vault, with heading-link repair and an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]inventory report.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Capture grammar, spans, typing rewrite, and NOTES routing for [bold white on #D75F87][/bold #D7AFFF] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]requirements[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]capture-reqs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after block-layout[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-reqs: admit requirement bullets at every eligible capture [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]position and depth, add refusals, the req_marker span, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]expand_req_marker rewrite, NOTES routing with the first-requirement [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]scoop, and nested requirements in project-note capture; grammar revision[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]29.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Carry a requirement branch into its own task[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]req-split[dim] · [dim][/dim]after block-layout[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]req-split: extend Task Split to select requirements at any depth, move [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the whole branch with depth rebasing and the NOTES rule, leave a [>] [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stub, refuse overlaps and excluded rows, and expose a library entry with[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a move map.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Requirements on the capture successor card[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]close-engine[dim] · [dim][/dim]after reader-hardening, capture-reqs, req-split[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]close-engine: build per-owner requirement groups for managed Done [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]closes, the met/drop/carry/pull-in verdicts with overlap and staleness [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]refusals, CLI flags and the --req-choice gate, JSON and receipts, RV [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vectors, and §12 docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Render requirements in Obsidian[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ledger-marks[dim] · [dim][/dim]after req-contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ledger-marks: draw the depth-aware ⌗ run in the owner's ink in Live [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Preview and Reading view with state styling, hidden unclickable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]checkboxes, the session toggle, tooltips, and freshness guards in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob-ledger-tools.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Obsidian requirement guards, toggle, drop, and typing assist[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]obsidian-gestures[dim] · [dim][/dim]after reader-hardening, block-layout[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]obsidian-gestures: add recognizer and layout twins to the cycler and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav, guard every task gesture on requirement lines, add Ctrl+] toggling [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with zone placement, Alt+[ drop and Alt+] restore, the owner Task Card, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the offer-close scope fix, and the `- [` + space expansion with atomic [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Backspace.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Requirements on the Obsidian successor card and carry-now[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]obsidian-close-card[dim] · [dim][/dim]after close-engine, obsidian-gestures[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]obsidian-close-card: mirror the requirement split in nav with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]api.taskSplit, bind Ctrl+Shift+T carry-now on requirement lines, render [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]picker v6 requirement groups with their keys, and let the cycler plan [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and apply verdicts with guarded Undo.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  12 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Promotion maps requirements to tasks and notes to notes[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]promotion[dim] · [dim][/dim]after obsidian-close-card[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]promotion: rewrite nav's project seed so top-level requirements become [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]## Tasks rows that keep their nested requirements, notes and NOTES [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]become ## Notes even on requirement-less tasks, and the receipt counts [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]both.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  13 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Mac requirement typing and glyph overlay[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-authoring[dim] · [dim][/dim]after capture-reqs[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-authoring: apply bob's expand_req_marker natively with overtype [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]absorption, delete a requirement marker atomically, and draw the ⌗ run [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]over req_marker spans in Bob Mac Capture.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  14 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Mac bullet indentation beyond two levels[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-nesting[dim] · [dim][/dim]after mac-authoring[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-nesting: generalize Tab/Shift-Tab, Ctrl-J continuation, paste [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]placeholders, and empty-row deletion in Bob Mac Capture from the fixed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]0/2-space levels to any authored depth.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  15 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Requirements on the Mac Pull-In card[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-close-card[dim] · [dim][/dim]after close-engine, mac-nesting[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-close-card: decode requirement groups, carry them through every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]offer path, stage met/drop/carry/pull-in verdicts with overlap feedback,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and submit them behind --req-choice in Bob Mac Capture.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  16 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reviewed vault migration[/bold #D7AFFF]                                     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]vault-migration[dim] · [dim][/dim]after drawer-rename, ledger-marks, obsidian-gestures[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]vault-migration: gate `bob task rename-drawer REQUIREMENTS NOTES` and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]one `bob task tidy` pass through Bryan's approval, report Dataview TASK [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]queries without a #task filter, and prepare the opt-in requirement [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]review list.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  17 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Memory records for task requirements[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bol